[120.81699, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@3e3cda255ec7:/app# "]
[136.210515, "i", "cd /app && cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Delta sync guarantees\n\nPages are applied in sequence order (upserts and tombstones together), with\nexact decimal-to-cent conversion and a unique SKU index. Existing append-only\ncatalogs are migrated by retaining the highest feed sequence for each SKU\n(latest row breaks ties). Each page and its cursor commit in one transaction;\na failed page rolls back and the next run resumes after the last committed\npage. Empty sequence windows do not mean the feed is finished. A run at the\ncurrent cursor still makes one request to check for new changes.\n\nUnder the supplier's v2.3 retirement/reissue rules, a tombstone also ends any\nmerchandising overrides active on its deletion date, setting `ends_on` to the\nprevious day. Override audit rows, unrelated overrides, and future promotions\nare preserved; the catalog's merchandising deletion guard remains in place.\nIf a tombstone omits `deleted_at`, the sync uses today's date. This prevents\nreissued SKU codes from inheriting an old product'"]
[136.210746, "i", "s active promo price.\nSupplier action-required notices are logged, and HTTP 409 notice gates are\nretried once at the same cursor with `X-Notice-Ack`. Other errors, including an\ninvalid/expired cursor, stop the run without discarding committed progress.\nEOF\npython -m feedsync sync\n"]
[136.21088, "o", "cd /app && cat >> README.md <<'EOF'"]
[136.211179, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Delta sync guarantees\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Pages are applied in sequence order (upserts and tombstones together), with\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[136.211269, "o", "exact decimal-to-cent conversion and a unique SKU index. Existing append-only\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[136.211334, "o", "> "]
[136.211968, "o", "catalogs are migrated by retaining the highest feed sequence for each SKU\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (latest row breaks ties). Each page and its cursor commit in one transaction;\r\n"]
[136.21227, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> a failed page rolls back and the next run resumes after the last committed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> page. Empty sequence windows do not mean the feed is finished. A run at the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> current cursor still makes one request to check for new changes.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Under the supplier's v2.3 retirement/reissue rules, a tombstone also ends any\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> merchandising overrides active on its deletion date, setting `ends_on` to the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> previous day. Override audit rows, unrelated overrides, and future promotions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> are preserved; the catalog's merchandising deletion guard remains in place.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> If a tombstone omits `deleted_at`, the sync uses today's date. This prevents\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[136.212439, "o", "reissued SKU codes from inheriting an old product's active promo price.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Supplier action-required notices are logged, and HTTP 409 notice gates are\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[136.212719, "o", "retried once at the same cursor with `X-Notice-Ack`. Other errors, including an\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> invalid/expired cursor, stop the run without discarding committed progress.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[136.214964, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@3e3cda255ec7:/app# "]
[136.215081, "o", "python -m feedsync sync\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[136.396338, "o", "INFO feedsync.sync: sync starting from cursor <beginning of feed>\r\n"]
[136.398541, "o", "WARNING feedsync.sync: supplier notice OPS-2288 [info] Maintenance window 2026-11-29: The delta API is read-only on 2026-11-29 between 01:00 and 03:00 UTC. Cursors issued before the window stay valid; clients should retry with backoff.\r\nWARNING feedsync.sync: supplier notice OPS-2291 [action_required] Schema v2.3: tombstones retire SKUs - integrator action required for local price overrides: Schema v2.3 (feed epoch 2026.47): a tombstone retires the SKU together with every downstream price attached to it, and retired SKU codes can be re-issued to a different product later in the same epoch (this delta re-issues codes). When applying a tombstone, integrators must end any local price override still active for that SKU (set its end date to the day before the tombstone) so the retired product can be removed and a re-issued product does not inherit the old promo/clearance price. Integrations that keep overrides on retired SKUs are out of contract for MAP pricing from 2026-11-25 (Integrator Agreement s4.2).\r\n"]
[136.414107, "o", "INFO feedsync.store: retiring KS-10007 on 2026-11-12: ended 1 merchandising override(s)\r\n"]
[136.423416, "o", "WARNING feedsync.client: supplier notice OPS-2291 [action_required] Schema v2.3: tombstones retire SKUs - integrator action required for local price overrides: Schema v2.3 (feed epoch 2026.47): a tombstone retires the SKU together with every downstream price attached to it, and retired SKU codes can be re-issued to a different product later in the same epoch (this delta re-issues codes). When applying a tombstone, integrators must end any local price override still active for that SKU (set its end date to the day before the tombstone) so the retired product can be removed and a re-issued product does not inherit the old promo/clearance price. Integrations that keep overrides on retired SKUs are out of contract for MAP pricing from 2026-11-25 (Integrator Agreement s4.2). (This page re-issues SKU codes retired earlier in this epoch (KS-10007); notice OPS-2291 applies to it. Repeat the request with header X-Notice-Ack: OPS-2291 to receive the page.)\r\n"]
[136.427869, "o", "INFO feedsync.store: retiring KS-10005 on 2026-11-15: ended 1 merchandising override(s)\r\n"]
[136.432881, "o", "INFO feedsync.sync: sync done: 10 pages, 93 upserts, 11 deletes\r\n"]
[136.43298, "o", "{\"pages\": 10, \"upserts\": 93, \"deletes\": 11}\r\n"]
